What's the Short Version?
The Shipping Clerk verifies and accurately logs, invoices, tags, and loads shipments, including PSST and R&amp;L (if applicable) orders at a fast and accurate pace. This role interacts with customers and various internal departments. Employees are required to safely and efficiently load trailers and other vehicles, depending on Ship Via, by manually lifting and stacking cases of product.

What Will You Be Doing?
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Invoice, tag and load customer shipments in an accurate and timely manner.
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Verify orders and charges for accurate invoicing, tagging and loading shipments, including PSST and R&amp;L shipments.
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Create parcel or freight invoices with close attention to accuracy of shipping charges and deadlines.
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Respond to account executive, traffic, drivers, or other inquiries by phone or e-mail.
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Manually load pallets on conveyor by safely and efficiently lifting and stacking cases.
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Use Radio Frequency (RF) unit in combination with Internal Operating System to perform daily work.
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Use Internal Operating System to verify accuracy of shipping details.
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Meet minimum production and accuracy standards and delivery deadlines.
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Responsible for checking out equipment and returning in same condition.
• &nbsp; &nbsp;May be required to operate powered lift equipment which will require completion of SanMar’s Lift Operator Certification every three years.
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Maintain safe, neat and clean work area by adhering to SanMar’s safety regulations.
What Are We Looking For?
• &nbsp; &nbsp;High School Diploma or equivalent&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Less than 1 year of experience in a warehouse&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Ability to read, write and have sufficient ability to identify colors, sizes, quantity, label and SKU information&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Basic math skills in counting and quantity required&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Ability to work with customers and coworkers and keep a positive, supportive attitude towards the Company and job&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;May be required to complete and maintain SanMar’s Lift Operator Certification every three years&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Strong customer service skills&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Demonstrated verbal and written communication skills&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Excellent organization skills; demonstrating the ability to multi-task and prioritize daily responsibilities&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Ability to learn Internal Operating System(s) and operate Radio Frequency (RF) unit&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Self-starter with strong initiative and ability to work efficiently, with minimal supervision&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Strong attention to detail&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Proficient typing and data entry skills&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Demonstrates ability to follow directions and change priorities or job duties as business needs require&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Ability to work in high-demand, high-volume environment and meet deadlines&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Able to work both independently and within a team&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Essential days or overtime may be required&nbsp;

What's Our Offer?&nbsp;
Paid Time Off: You`ll accrue paid time off on a weekly basis based on hours worked up to 112 hours per year to start. Employees also receive 8 paid holidays and 1 paid family day off.

Additional Benefits:
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision benefits
