Roku is changing how the world watches TV

Roku is the #1 TV streaming platform in the U.S., Canada, and Mexico, and we've set our sights on powering every television in the world. Roku pioneered streaming to the TV. Our mission is to be the TV streaming platform that connects the entire TV ecosystem. We connect consumers to the content they love, enable content publishers to build and monetize large audiences, and provide advertisers unique capabilities to engage consumers.

From your first day at Roku, you'll make a valuable - and valued - contribution. We're a fast-growing public company where no one is a bystander. We offer you the opportunity to delight millions of TV streamers around the world while gaining meaningful experience across a variety of disciplines.

&nbsp;

About the role&nbsp;

Roku is looking for an Associate General Counsel, Privacy &amp; Litigation to join our Legal team. This role owns Roku’s litigation portfolio outside of intellectual property matters - including consumer class actions, commercial disputes, and government investigations, with a particular focus on privacy-related litigation and related regulatory enforcement actions - across a business that spans hardware, streaming, and one of the fastest-growing advertising platforms in media.&nbsp;

You will manage disputes and government inquiries end-to-end, from first notice through resolution&nbsp;- building the strategy, directing outside counsel, and making the call on when to fight, settle, or escalate. This role reports to the VP, Deputy General Counsel, Strategic&nbsp;Litigation&nbsp;and IP.&nbsp;

We think of running a case as a creative act, not just a process. The matters that land here rarely come with a clean playbook - the facts are&nbsp;incomplete,&nbsp;the law is unsettled, or the right answer just&nbsp;isn’t&nbsp;obvious yet. We’re looking for someone who is energized by that kind of ambiguity: who can construct a novel argument or a case theory nobody else saw, stay clear-headed when a matter is genuinely indeterminate, and write their way to a conclusion -&nbsp;briefs,&nbsp;internal memos, demand letters, whatever the moment calls for - with the kind of clarity and force that changes how people see the case.&nbsp;

The estimated annual base salary for this position is between $270,000 and $300,000 with additional equity. Compensation packages are based on factors unique to each candidate, including but not limited to skill set, certifications, and specific geographic location. This role is eligible for health insurance, equity awards, life insurance, disability benefits, parental leave, wellness benefits, and paid time off.

This position will be based in Austin, TX and will be in office Monday - Thursday with the option to work from home on Friday.

